This attribute is used to specify multiple benchmarks. It accepts the same parameters as the #[bench] attribute: args, config, setup and teardown and additionally the iter and file parameters which are explained in full detail in Specifying multiple benchmarks at once . In contrast to the args parameter in #[bench] , args takes an array of arguments. # extern crate gungraun;
# mod my_lib { pub fn bubble_sort(value: Vec<i32>) -> Vec<i32> { value } }
use gungraun::{library_benchmark, library_benchmark_group, main, LibraryBenchmarkConfig};
