Flamegraphs are opt-in and can be created if you pass a FlamegraphConfig to the BinaryBenchmarkConfig or LibraryBenchmarkConfig. Callgrind flamegraphs are meant as a complement to valgrind's visualization tools callgrind_annotate and kcachegrind. For example create all kind of flamegraphs for all benchmarks in a library benchmark: # extern crate gungraun;
# mod my_lib { pub fn bubble_sort(_: Vec<i32>) -> Vec<i32> { vec![] } }
use gungraun::{ library_benchmark, library_benchmark_group, main, LibraryBenchmarkConfig, FlamegraphConfig, Callgrind
};
use std::hint::black_box; #[library_benchmark]
fn bench_library() -> Vec<i32> { black_box(my_lib::bubble_sort(vec![3, 2, 1]))
} library_benchmark_group!(name = my_group; benchmarks = bench_library); # fn main() {
main!( config = LibraryBenchmarkConfig::default() .tool(Callgrind::default() .flamegraph(FlamegraphConfig::default()) ); library_benchmark_groups = my_group
);
# } The produced flamegraph *.svg files are located next to the respective callgrind output file in the target/gungraun directory .
